\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O God, my God, my all Thou art:
\par Ere shines the dawn of rising day;
\par Thy sovereign light within my heart,
\par Thy all-enlivening power display.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. For Thee my thirsty soul doth pant,
\par While in this desert land I live;
\par And hungry as I am, and faint,
\par Thy love alone can comfort give.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. In a dry land, behold, I place
\par My whole desire on Thee, O Lord;
\par And more I joy to gain Thy grace,
\par Than all earth's treasures can afford.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. More dear than life itself, Thy love
\par My heart and tongue shall still employ;
\par And to declare Thy praise will prove
\par My peace, my glory, and my joy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. In blessing Thee, with grateful songs
\par My happy life shall glide away;
\par The praise that to Thy name belongs
\par Hourly with lifted hands I'll pay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thy name, O God, upon my bed
\par Dwells on my lips, and fires my thought;
\par WIth trembling awe, in midnight shade,
\par I muse on all Thy hands have wrought.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. In all I do I feel Thine aid;
\par Therefore Thy greatness will I sing,
\par O God, who bidd'st my heart be glad
\par Beneath the shadow of Thy wing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. My soul draws nigh and cleaves to Thee:
\par Then let or earth or hell assail,
\par Thy mighty hand shall set me free;
\par For whom Thou sav'st, he ne'er shall fail.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

